[[7028,2707,"The care management and treatment of this child on the innumerable occasions she presented with an exacerbation of asthma, was centred solely on treating the immediate presentation as an isolated acute event seeking its stabilisation and returning her to the care of her family.","lack of long term management of asthma",""],[7029,2707,"No co-ordinating record of these occasions","lack of coordinated record keeping",""],[7030,2707,"No analysis of the frequency or circumstances of the events","lack of event frequency analysis",""],[7031,2707,"No analysis of the medication or level of medication prescribed","lack of medication level analysis",""],[7032,2707,"No determination of its effectiveness the frequency or regularity of its use","lack of effectiveness determination",""],[7033,2707,"No appreciation of the deteriorating nature of her respiratory condition","lack of deterioration appreciation",""],[7808,2996,"The deceased underwent an elective reversal in January 2013 of an illiostomy performed in 2007 due to a cancer within the lower bowel","dehisence of bowel anastomosis leading to internal infection",""],[7809,2996,"The care plan devised during this period of community nursing care did identify a need to record temperature and blood pressure readings. Unfortunately these readings were not carried out and accordingly were not recorded","lack of vital sign monitoring",""],[7810,2996,"Surgical patients discharged to the community should be accompanied by a clear and direct plan for their expected level of care in the community","inadequate discharge planning",""],[7811,2996,"The recording of the deceased' vital signs, temperature and blood pressure would have provided some insight into the deceased' wellbeing and possibly given an early indication of a developing crisis","missed early warning signs",""],[7812,2996,"It is potentially possible to have been continuing in some degree for some considerable time","undetected ongoing bowel dehiscence",""],[7813,2996,"Failure to maintain records, thereafter to properly interpret and action them, can it must be remembered be a basis for legal both Civil and Criminal","inadequate record keeping",""]]